  "title": "Kate Sheppard",
  "summary": "Kate Sheppard, born in Liverpool in 1847, settled in Christchurch and led the franchise campaign for women's suffrage in New Zealand. Her last petition, in 1893, carried nearly 32,000 signatures, and the Electoral Act 1893 giving women the vote was passed on 19 September 1893. She died in Riccarton, Christchurch, on 13 July 1934.",
